<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 584 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 584 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 584 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>The central bank said the assistance comprised 59 million stg of outright bill purchases maturing on or before March 24 and 525 million stg at the established repo rate of 6.0 percent. The repos mature March 21 and March 24.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
